# `is_empty` returning `false` unconditionally, which it already does.
#
# `Buffer::new` is the only constructor, and it sizes its slots to
# `capacity.get()`. `Capacity` is a newtype whose only `Self( .. )` sits past a
# rejection of zero, so every `Capacity` is at least one and every `Buffer` has
# at least one slot. `is_empty` therefore returns `false` for every value of the
# type that can exist, and a mutant returning `false` returns the same answer.
#
# This is an equivalent mutant rather than a blind spot: no test can kill it,
# because no test can build the input that would separate it from the original.
# The crate already knew. The test covering this line is named
# `a_buffer_is_never_empty_because_a_capacity_is_never_zero`.
#
# Five sibling crates carried a *real* one-polarity defect on their own
# `is_empty` in the same sweep and are held by `mutant/S2` through `S6`. That
# this one looks identical and is not is the reason both directories exist.

ring_store/src/lib.rs:182:5: replace Buffer<S>::is_empty -> bool with false
